    "etymology": {
     "text": "Phono-semantic compound: semantic 水 (‘water’) + phonetic; the character’s old meaning is ‘to sink’. The negator méi is possibly a colloquial variant of 勿 or 未 influenced by 有 — not derived from ‘to sink’ (Schuessler).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "The traditional form 沒 has 𠬛 on the right; the simplified 没 writes 殳 (几 over 又) instead."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "Never *没是 — the negation of 是 is 不是.",
     "Don’t add 了 after 没 + verb: 我没吃 (not *我没吃了).",
     "In 沉没 (chénmò, ‘to sink’) the same character is read mò."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "没 describes facts, 不 describes will and habits: 我不吃肉 ‘I don’t eat meat’ vs 我没吃肉 ‘I didn’t eat (the) meat’."
    ]
